---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="License Agreement (EULA) — Zarlino Audio"
  description="The end-user licence agreement that governs use of Zarlino Audio software."
  canonicalURL="https://zarlinoaudio.com/legal/license"
  schemaType="website"
>
  <main class="relative z-[1] bg-[#050505] min-h-screen pt-24 pb-24 px-6 md:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[820px] mx-auto">
      <nav class="mb-8 font-['Inter'] text-[13px] text-[#64748B]">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Zarlino Audio</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#94A3B8]">License Agreement</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[clamp(32px,4.5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.02em]">
        License Agreement (EULA)
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 font-['IBM_Plex_Mono'] text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[#64748B]">
        Version 1.0 · 2 October 2026
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 font-['Inter'] text-[16px] text-[#94A3B8] leading-[1.8] space-y-8">
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">1. Licence grant</h2>
          <p>
            When you buy a Zarlino Audio plugin, we grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
            perpetual licence to install and use that plugin, for a single user, on computers you own
            or control, for your own music production and post-production work. You may make backup
            copies of the installer and your licence key.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">2. What you may not do</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Resell, rent, lease, sublicense, share, or publicly post licence keys.</li>
            <li>Redistribute, publish, or make the software available to third parties.</li>
            <li>Remove or alter copyright, licence, or attribution notices.</li>
            <li>Bypass, disable, or extract the licence or activation functionality.</li>
            <li>Reverse engineer or decompile the software, except to the extent expressly permitted by applicable law.</li>
            <li>Use the software in violation of any applicable law.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">3. Trial &amp; beta builds</h2>
          <p>
            Demo/trial functionality runs for 14 days without a licence. "Public beta" builds are
            provided as-is for evaluation and normal use, are subject to change, and may contain
            defects; keep backups of your projects as you normally would.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">4. Ownership</h2>
          <p>
            The software, its design, and its documentation remain owned by Zarlino Audio and its
            licensors. The software includes components of the JUCE framework and other third-party
            or open-source libraries, each governed by their own licences, which we comply with.
            This agreement gives you a licence to use the software — not ownership of it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">5. Termination</h2>
          <p>
            This licence ends automatically if you materially breach it. On termination you must stop
            using and delete the software. Termination does not affect your rights under the Refund
            Policy or applicable consumer law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">6. Warranty &amp; liability</h2>
          <p>
            The software is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind, to the extent the law
            allows. To the extent the law allows, our total liability arising out of or relating to
            the software is limited to the amount you paid for it, and we are not liable for indirect
            or consequential losses, including lost profits or lost or corrupted project data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">7. Governing law</h2>
          <p>
            This agreement is governed by the laws of Ghana. Contact:{' '}
            <a href="mailto:support@zarlinoaudio.com" class="text-[#00D4FF] hover:underline">support@zarlinoaudio.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p class="pt-4 border-t border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.06)] text-[13px] text-[#475569]">
          Plain-language version 1.0 — pending legal review. We will publish an updated version once reviewed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
